.TH PLANK-TABLET-RELAY-ADMIN 8 "September 2026" "PLANK" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
plank-tablet-relay-admin \- recover tablet relay pairing over SSH
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plank-tablet-relay-admin reset-headsets --yes
.br
.B plank-tablet-relay-admin remove-tablet
.I Bluetooth-address
.B --yes
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run as root to recover access when normal headset-app management is unavailable.
The command stops the relay, locks its saved state, performs the selected
operation, and restarts the relay if it was previously running.
.PP
reset-headsets revokes approved headset keys while retaining the relay identity
and tablet bonds. Forget the local relay pairing in the app before approving
the headset again with three tablet-button presses.
.PP
remove-tablet removes only the selected saved Wacom Bluetooth bond and its
tablet selection. Other tablet bonds and headset approvals remain intact.
It refuses unrelated Bluetooth devices.
.PP
Previous enrollment metadata is saved privately under
/var/backups/plank-tablet-relay. This is not a backup of deleted Bluetooth keys.
Normal sleep or disconnection does not require either recovery command.
.SH FILES
/etc/plank-tablet-relay-ble/relay.conf
.br
/var/lib/plank-tablet-relay-ble
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR plank-tablet-relay-ble (1),
.BR bluetoothctl (1)
